The license does not claim ownership over the inalienable right to pursue happiness itself. It covers Branton Allan Baker's authored expression, wording, documentation, examples, prompts, source code, implementations, and applied framework around the restored definition of that right.

Decision Filter Coverage

Use of the inalienable right to pursue happiness as a decision filter is a covered use of the Concept Principle.

A decision filter is any rule, prompt, policy, check, gate, evaluator, review process, approval process, routing rule, access rule, audit rule, or behavioral standard that applies the Concept Principle to a request, output, policy, system behavior, product feature, or human or machine decision.

This coverage applies even if the decision filter is renamed, paraphrased, translated, embedded in code, embedded in prompts, embedded in documentation, or presented under another project name.

